      "content": "While the scale of expansion is undeniable, concluding that the *volume* itself is the sole cause requires further rigorous analysis to separate correlation from causation. Attributing workforce withdrawal solely to the size of the net ignores the potential positive impacts, such as improved health or better education that actually *enables* better labor force participation later on. The debate often lies in how the programs are *structured*—the benefit phase-outs, the eligibility rules, and the support services are more critical than the raw spending number.",
